    "answer": {
      "short": "15; the two-digit multiples of 6 run from $6\\times2=12$ to $6\\times16=96$.",
      "worked": "A number divisible by both 2 and 3 is divisible by 6. The first two-digit multiple is $6\\times2=12$, and the last is $6\\times16=96$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of multiples}&=16-2+1\\\\&=15\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
